When you’re creating a product survey, it’s important to ask questions that will give you insight into what your customers think about the product. One important question to ask is “Is there anything you don’t like about the product?”

This question can be very helpful in understanding customer sentiment about the product. It can also help you identify areas where the product could be improved.

If you have a lot of customers who respond negatively to this question, it could be an indication that there are serious problems with the product. In this case, it would be important to take action to address the issues that were raised.

On the other hand, if only a small number of customers mention problems with the product, it could be that the issues are not widespread. In this case, you might decide to take no action or only make minor changes to the product.', ARRAY['Product Survey Questions Guide', 'Here Are The Questions You Need To Ask', 'Is there anything you don’t like about the product?']::text[], '### Is there anything you don’t like about the product?

