CES is an important event for startups because it can help them learn what customers want. This information can be used to validate a product idea and to make connections with potential investors and customers. Additionally, CES can provide startups with insights into the latest trends in technology. By attending CES, startups can stay ahead of the curve and gain an advantage in the market.

Attending CES can also help to build a company''s brand. By exhibiting at the event, startups can connect with potential customers and partners. This exposure can give a startup an advantage over similar businesses. Additionally, by attending various events during CES, startups can gain insights into different markets and industries. By learning about these sectors, startups can better understand what customers want and how to meet their needs.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide For Customer Effort Score (CES)', 'What Is A Customer Effort Score (CES)?', 'Why Is CES Important For Startups?']::text[], '### Why Is CES Important For Startups?

