The Customer Effort Score (CES) is a metric that measures how much effort a customer has put into interacting with your company. It is essential to have a high CES because it shows that you are providing good customer service. There are many ways to increase your CES, and this article will discuss three of the most common methods.

The first way to increase your CES is by ensuring that you have clear and concise customer instructions. This will help customers understand what they need to do to receive assistance from your company. In addition, it will reduce the time customers spend trying to figure out how to use your products or services.

Another way to increase your CES is by providing quality feedback. This includes not only giving feedback on product features but also giving feedback on customer interactions. You can help customers learn from their mistakes and improve their overall experience with your company by providing quality feedback.

The final method for increasing your CES is by responding quickly to customer requests. This means responding within a reasonable timeframe and promptly addressing any issues raised. By doing this, you can ensure that customers feel like they are getting the support they need from your company and that their needs are being met promptly and efficiently.', NULL, false, 88, '1.3.0', '00a145d9-3587-45a5-b87b-6d7c819b95e9', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', false, '');
