When it comes to customer satisfaction, there are two main metrics that businesses look at: NPS and CSAT. While they have some similarities, their differences are important to consider.

NPS is a longer-term metric while CSAT is a shorter-term metric. NPS measures customer loyalty over a period of time (typically 3 or 6 months), while CSAT measures customer satisfaction with a recent interaction. This means that NPS can be used to predict future business growth, while CSAT can be used to identify areas of improvement within the customer experience.

The two metrics are not mutually exclusive and can be used together to get a more holistic view of the customer. For example, if you know that 70% of your customers are satisfied with their recent interactions but you want to know what’s causing this dissatisfaction, you could combine NPS data with feedback from frontline workers in order to find out where improvements need to be made.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide For Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT)', 'Defining Your Customer Satisfaction Score (CSAT)', 'The Difference Between NPS And CSAT']::text[], '### The Difference Between NPS And CSAT

