# Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)

In this blog post, we''ve provided a basic overview of what NPS is and how to calculate it. We''ve also covered some of its advantages and how to use it to improve your business. Read On!

The Net Promoter Score, or NPS, is a customer satisfaction metric that measures how likely your customers are to recommend your business to others. It''s a simple yet powerful way to gauge customer satisfaction and loyalty, and it can be a valuable tool for businesses of all sizes. In this blog post, we''ll give you a crash course in all things NPS. We''ll cover everything from the basics of what NPS is to its advantages and how to calculate your own NPS. We''ll even touch on how to analyze and follow up with your NPS results. By the end of this post, you should have a good understanding of NPS and how it can benefit your business.', ARRAY[]::text[], '- Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)', NULL, false, 228, '1.3.0', 'a0538131-821b-4169-9c78-99126645e929', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', false, '');
INSERT INTO askcontent."document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('614b6e5a-b1ce-4901-bda6-de617e10da04', 'b6f0616b-6a54-4fe2-986a-0f7f84515366', 'chk_6e0b2d432da6fe41', 1, '### What Is NPS?

NPS is a metric that measures customer satisfaction and engagement. It can be used to identify promoters, detractors, and passives. Additionally, it can be used to calculate the Net Promoter Score. The Net Promoter Score is a valuable metric for measuring customer satisfaction and can provide insights into how well a company is doing in retaining customers.

Promoters are those customers who have high levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services. Detractors are those customers who have low levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services. Passives are those customers who neither have high nor low levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services but do not contribute to evangelism either way. Calculating NPS involves calculating the percentage of respondents in each category, then adding them up to create a total score for the entire group of respondents. The higher the score, the more satisfied and engaged customers are with the company''s products or services.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)', 'What Is NPS?']::text[], '### What Is NPS?

NPS is a metric that measures customer satisfaction and engagement. It can be used to identify promoters, detractors, and passives. Additionally, it can be used to calculate the Net Promoter Score. The Net Promoter Score is a valuable metric for measuring customer satisfaction and can provide insights into how well a company is doing in retaining customers.

Promoters are those customers who have high levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services. Detractors are those customers who have low levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services. Passives are those customers who neither have high nor low levels of satisfaction with the company''s products or services but do not contribute to evangelism either way. Calculating NPS involves calculating the percentage of respondents in each category, then adding them up to create a total score for the entire group of respondents. The higher the score, the more satisfied and engaged customers are with the company''s products or services.

NPS has been shown to be an effective tool for assessing customer satisfaction and engagement within companies. By understanding which groups of customers are most satisfied with their interactions with a given business, managers can focus their marketing efforts on reaching these consumers more effectively.', NULL, false, 259, '1.3.0', 'a88262bf-48bc-4b7a-aebe-5a04a0f3eb62', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', false, '');
