INSERT INTO askcontent."document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('614b6e5a-b1ce-4901-bda6-de617e10da04', 'b6f0616b-6a54-4fe2-986a-0f7f84515366', 'chk_8da10f54ab5aacc8', 3, '### The Benefits Of NPS

Net Promoter Score, or NPS, has been growing in popularity as a way to measure customer loyalty and satisfaction. NPS is a simple rating system that takes into account how likely people are to recommend a company to others, on a scale from 0 (not at all likely) to 10 (extremely likely).

Tracking customer loyalty through NPS can be valuable for businesses in several ways. First of all, it can help identify areas where improvement is needed. For example, if the average NPS score for a certain product category is 6 but the score for that category falls below 5 after an update has been released, this may indicate that there are problems with that product. By understanding these problems early on, companies can address them quickly and improve customer loyalty at the same time.

Another benefit of tracking customer loyalty through NPS is that it can be used as a predictor of growth. Companies with high NPS scores tend to experience faster growth than those with lower scores over time. This suggests that measuring customer satisfaction through NPS could be one way to predict future success for businesses.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)', 'What Is NPS?', 'The Benefits Of NPS']::text[], '### The Benefits Of NPS

Net Promoter Score, or NPS, has been growing in popularity as a way to measure customer loyalty and satisfaction. NPS is a simple rating system that takes into account how likely people are to recommend a company to others, on a scale from 0 (not at all likely) to 10 (extremely likely).

Tracking customer loyalty through NPS can be valuable for businesses in several ways. First of all, it can help identify areas where improvement is needed. For example, if the average NPS score for a certain product category is 6 but the score for that category falls below 5 after an update has been released, this may indicate that there are problems with that product. By understanding these problems early on, companies can address them quickly and improve customer loyalty at the same time.

Another benefit of tracking customer loyalty through NPS is that it can be used as a predictor of growth. Companies with high NPS scores tend to experience faster growth than those with lower scores over time. This suggests that measuring customer satisfaction through NPS could be one way to predict future success for businesses.

Finally, measuring customer satisfaction through NPS can also help companies understand their customers better. By understanding which aspects of the business are important to customers, companies can create products or services that cater specifically to those needs. In short, by using NPS data wisely, businesses can achieve many benefits related to customer retention and growth.', NULL, false, 285, '1.3.0', '81a79266-72ee-4be3-a553-f0e7b499267f', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', false, '');
