If you''re looking to improve your customer service, you need to calculate your NPS (Net Promoter Score). Your NPS is a metric that gauges the level of satisfaction of customers with your company. It''s important to know how to calculate it and find the reason for each score. You can also use Text AI to analyze your data and learn more about how customers interact with your company.

Your NPS is determined by calculating the percentage of customers who give your company a rating of ''promoters'' or ''detractors.'' To get this score, divide the total number of customers who gave your company a rating of 5 or 4 stars by the total number of customers. The resulting number is your NPS.

NPS ranges from 0 to 100, where 0 indicates that no one is satisfied and 100 indicates that everyone is satisfied. A score above 50 indicates that more than half of your customers are promoters, while a score below 30 indicates that more than three-quarters of your customers are detractors.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)', 'What Is NPS?', 'How To Calculate Your NPS']::text[], '### How To Calculate Your NPS

If you''re looking to improve your customer service, you need to calculate your NPS (Net Promoter Score). Your NPS is a metric that gauges the level of satisfaction of customers with your company. It''s important to know how to calculate it and find the reason for each score. You can also use Text AI to analyze your data and learn more about how customers interact with your company.

Your NPS is determined by calculating the percentage of customers who give your company a rating of ''promoters'' or ''detractors.'' To get this score, divide the total number of customers who gave your company a rating of 5 or 4 stars by the total number of customers. The resulting number is your NPS.

NPS ranges from 0 to 100, where 0 indicates that no one is satisfied and 100 indicates that everyone is satisfied. A score above 50 indicates that more than half of your customers are promoters, while a score below 30 indicates that more than three-quarters of your customers are detractors.

There are several reasons why customer satisfaction can change over time. Some factors that can affect satisfaction include how you communicate with customers, what services you offer, how easy it is to find information about your company, and whether you respond quickly to customer complaints. You can use Text AI to monitor these changes in customer satisfaction and make adjustments as needed.', NULL, false, 252, '1.3.0', '9a1ea92a-0ea9-4dfc-b793-24191ec98e5c', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', '2026-08-23 15:16:23.389988+00:00', false, '');
