The reason behind your scores can help you to improve your business. For example, if you have a Net Promoter Score (NPS) that is lower than desirable, it may be useful to understand why this is the case. Knowing what promoters and detractors are likely to do can help you to focus on those who will support your business, and avoid engagement with detractors.

Text AI can also be helpful in understanding customer feedback. This technology can analyze large amounts of text data and identify key phrases or themes. From here, it can provide insights into how customers are feeling about your product or service. Customer follow up is essential in order for businesses to maintain relationships with their customers; without it, there is a risk of losing valuable customer data.

One of the most important things that businesses can do to improve their scores is to understand their customer base. This means understanding what customers like and don’t like, as well as how they use your product or service. Knowing which features are popular can help you to focus on developing these for future releases. It is also important to follow up with customers who have left negative feedback – doing so will show that you are taking their feedback seriously, and allow them to feel appreciated. Additionally, it can encourage them to return in the future.', ARRAY['Ultimate Guide To Net Promoter Score (NPS)', 'What Is NPS?', 'The Reasons Behind Your Scores']::text[], '### The Reasons Behind Your Scores

